class:: Onsets2
summary:: Causal flux and SuperFlux-style onset evidence
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets

description::
Returns an onset trigger and a continuously decaying onset-strength value. code::\flux:: uses absolute log-spectral difference, code::\fluxPos:: keeps increases, and code::\superflux:: compares increases against a maximum-filtered neighborhood in the preceding log spectrum. A causal exponentially weighted mean and variance supply the adaptive threshold, and code::minGap:: suppresses clustered triggers.

The FFT hop must match code::hop:: so time constants remain correct. The first frame and silence return zero. It is practically similar to link::Classes/Onsets::, but exposes continuous strength, a SuperFlux-style option, seconds-based state, and explicit FFT/hop configuration; it is not numerically equivalent to the legacy detector.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize:: and code::hop::.

argument:: threshold
Nonnegative multiplier on the running onset-strength deviation.

argument:: method
Literal code::\flux::, code::\fluxPos::, or code::\superflux::.

argument:: relaxTime
Decay time in seconds for the strength output.

argument:: minGap
Minimum interval between triggers in seconds.

argument:: medianTime
History time in seconds for the causal adaptive mean and variance. The name preserves the planned interface, but version 0.1 uses exponential statistics rather than a literal median.

argument:: maxFilterBins
Literal frequency-neighborhood radius from 0 through 12 for code::\superflux::.

argument:: floor
Positive floor before the natural logarithm.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

argument:: hop
FFT hop as a fraction of code::fftSize::, from 0.0625 through 1.

returns::
An Array: trigger and nonnegative strength.

instancemethods::

examples::
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, 0.3, \superflux, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.5);
        var click = Decay2.ar(K2A.ar(onset[0]), 0.001, 0.04) * PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
        (source * 0.12 + click) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

